KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a non-empty hazard pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Hazard pointers ([saferecl.hp]): make_hazard_pointer returns a non-empty
one.  No standard library implements it yet (libstdc++ 16, libc++ 18), so the
test is written to N5008 and not checked with a compiler; it is FUTURE
until a library provides the header.  Then it is a KNOWNBUG or CORE
test of CBMC's support of that library code.
